              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "نهر (nahr) — \"a stream, a brook; a channel\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "کنار نهر نشستیم و چای خوردیم. Kenâr-e nahr neshastim va chây khordim. We sat by the stream and drank tea."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In Arabic nahr is a river; in Persian a smaller stream."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "nahr was borrowed from Arabic nahr 'river' (EtymDB); in Persian it names a stream or a channel."
            }
          ]
        },
